== 4b. THE AVERAGE LOOP'S RESPONSE (SNVSAI1D 7.3.4 and 7.3.6; CSS 47 nF, gm 1 mS, VSS(CL) 1.21 V, VREF 0.8 V) -- INFERRED from those parameters, the sheet states no time constant
  intrinsic time constant CSS / gm = 47.0 us
  onset: the gm amplifier must pull SS from its 1.21 V clamp to VREF 0.8 V before the output starts to fall; net pulldown = gm x (V_isns - V_target)
  overdrive   0.3 mV (0.05 A over the point on 6 mOhm): onset    64.23 ms, then the output falls at about   40.6 V/s
  overdrive   1.0 mV (0.17 A over the point on 6 mOhm): onset    19.27 ms, then the output falls at about  135.3 V/s
  overdrive   3.4 mV (0.57 A over the point on 6 mOhm): onset     5.67 ms, then the output falls at about  460.1 V/s
  overdrive  10.4 mV (1.73 A over the point on 6 mOhm): onset     1.85 ms, then the output falls at about 1407.3 V/s
  overdrive  20.0 mV (3.33 A over the point on 6 mOhm): onset     0.96 ms, then the output falls at about 2706.4 V/s
  => onset in milliseconds to tens of milliseconds, the fall to the loads' 4.6 V floor in milliseconds more: every PS-ALLTX burst (LoRa packet, Iridium session, a 60 s key-down) is longer, so burst duration does not keep the loop out; only the current does
  => bucks and LDOs behind the rail draw MORE input current as the rail falls (constant power), so the fold-back is regenerative until an eFuse's or a buck's UVLO opens: the brown-out of the always-on fabric S-99 names

