== 5. THE OPTIONS
  Option A, re-rate the average loop with a 5 mOhm ISNS shunt (the same WSL2512 family):
    5.0 mOhm: loop 8.51 / 10.00 / 11.52 A; the maximum against the lead's 10 A: 1.52 A FAIL (over the contact rating in a B-side fault held by a CCM stage with no hiccup)
    5.6 mOhm: loop 7.60 / 8.93 / 10.28 A; the maximum against the lead's 10 A: 0.28 A FAIL (over the contact rating in a B-side fault held by a CCM stage with no hiccup)
    => the 6 mOhm value is pinned by the lead's 10 A (the generator's own reason); re-rating alone fails the downstream test at the lead
  Option B, the D8 mezzanine on its own buck from VBAT (TPS62933, C3200405, fitted twice on this board; XAL6060-682ME Isat 9.2 A above the part's 5.8 A maximum high-side limit):
    tier D  demand 6.90 A: vs loop min PASS 0.16 A, vs typ PASS 1.43 A
    tier M  demand 5.94 A: vs loop min PASS 1.11 A, vs typ PASS 2.39 A
    tier Mx demand 5.94 A: vs loop min PASS 1.11 A, vs typ PASS 2.39 A
    tier P  demand 8.15 A: vs loop min FAIL -1.09 A, vs typ PASS 0.19 A
    the new buck at 2.0 A (U23's limit): ripple 1.04 A at 16.8 V and 500 kHz on 6.8 uH, peak 2.52 A against IHS_LIMIT min 4.2 A and Isat 9.2 A: PASS; VBAT +0.91 A at 12.4 V
  Option C, B plus the wall host port on the outlet interlock (U26's spare section 1: USBX_EN_HW = USBX_EN AND OUTLET_OK):
    tier D  demand 6.00 A: vs loop min PASS 1.06 A
    tier M  demand 5.44 A: vs loop min PASS 1.61 A
    tier P  demand 7.22 A: vs loop min FAIL -0.16 A
  Option D, declare the 8.9 A bound and name the fold-back as the limiter (cx1's third option): leaves REQ-018's 'every rail in regulation' unmet on the record; not an engineering option
  Option E, re-allocate D8 or the wall port to +5V_S1 or +5V_S3 (AP64500, 5 A): S1 reads 4.65 A PLAN in PS-ALLTX (PWR-F02, 7 percent margin), S3 about 4.2 A with its card off (cx1): no headroom for 1.5 to 2.0 A; rejected

== 6. RECOMMENDATION (authority SESSION, the two-part test in ANALYSIS.md section 5)
  Take option B now: the coincident demand on +5V_DEV returns to B + wall = 6.9 A declared (the present 6.9 A declaration becomes true), 5.94 A at the M-tier, under the loop's minimum with 0.16 and 1.11 A in hand;
  the P-tier (8.15 A) stays FAIL by 1.09 A and is board B's declarations to reconcile (S-98) and the bench to measure; option C is the fallback that buys 0.93 A more if the bench asks for it.
